European Industrial Gases Association. *Guideline for Safe Practices for Cryogenic Air Separation Plants*, Doc 147/22, revision of 147/20. [Complete official 85-page guide](https://www.eiga.eu/uploads/documents/DOC147.pdf).

Read the whole guide alongside the cryogenic course. Intake-air quality, compression, contaminant removal, expanders, pumps and the coldbox lead into controls, product handling, utilities, piping, shutdown, inspection, operations and training. Use the explanations to trace how an impurity or equipment change propagates through a real process; derive balances separately.

The cover, revision, contents and selected air-contaminant-removal, maintenance, commissioning, shift-handover and change-management passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. Different purification arrangements remove different contaminants, and some residuals require additional treatment elsewhere in the process. Historical designs and guidance have their stated scope.

